# 301 redirects for bug URLs that older builds of this site generated.
#
# These paths never had real pages — they were artifacts of relative-link bugs
# in the old build pipeline (browsers / Google's crawler concatenated a
# sibling-relative href onto the current page's directory URL, producing
# nonsense paths like /faq/docs/privacy/ which is really /docs/privacy/).
#
# The link-generation bugs were fixed in PR #2 (build.js absolute-URL fix), so
# nothing on the site points to these URLs anymore — but external sites and
# Google's index can still hold references for a long time. These redirects
# bridge the gap, sending any visitor or crawler that hits a bug URL to the
# real page they meant.
#
# When Google re-crawls and stops referencing these URLs entirely, the
# redirects can stay (cheap insurance) or be deleted in a future cleanup.
#
# Format: [from] [to] [status]

# Sibling-link bug from /faq/does-it-send-data-anywhere/ → another faq page
/faq/does-it-send-data-anywhere/how-does-it-handle-artifacts/  /faq/how-does-it-handle-artifacts/  301

# Cross-doc relative-link bugs: a /faq/ or /docs/ page linked to a /docs/ or
# /spec/ target with a sibling-relative href, so the crawler concatenated it
# onto the current directory (e.g. /faq/spec/markdown-format/, really
# /spec/markdown-format/). There are NO real pages under /faq/spec/,
# /docs/spec/, or /faq/docs/ — every path under them is a bug pointing at a
# real page one level up. Splat the whole prefix so we catch every spec/doc
# variant (markdown-format, html-format, console-snippet, the /spec/ index, …)
# instead of enumerating one at a time and waiting for Google to surface the
# next miss. An empty splat (/faq/spec/ → /spec/) lands on the /spec/ index,
# which exists. /docs/features/* stays enumerated below because /docs/features/
# is itself a real page — a splat there would clobber it.
/faq/spec/*   /spec/:splat   301
/docs/spec/*  /spec/:splat   301
/faq/docs/*   /docs/:splat   301

# Sibling-link bugs from /docs/features/ → other /docs/ siblings
/docs/features/pricing/         /docs/pricing/          301
/docs/features/changelog/       /docs/changelog/        301
/docs/features/privacy/         /docs/privacy/          301
/docs/features/getting-started/ /docs/getting-started/  301
